Common misconception, but yes, wearing the Eye only provides you with
ESP on top of its other benefits. Just carrying it in open inventory
provides magic resistance, half spell damage, and vastly improved mana
regeneration.  It should really be called the Eye of the Awesome. (note:
not really) When you have an amulet of lifesaving, you should be wearing
that instead.

Also remember that you can #invoke the Eye (and you don't need to be
wearing it for this either!) in order to branchport to any branch of
the dungeon that you've already been to. Great for luring wraiths,
sokoban stash management, &c. 

While some players do value ESP very highly (and there are good reasons
for that), on a first ascension I would strongly recommend lifesaving 
in favor of wearing the Eye. 

